old='A threshold comparison is not an audit-election approval.'
new='''**Selected statutory-incorporation reading for an ordinary cash-funded Sp/F:** §33 expressly allows premium to be paid in the same proportion as the subscribed capital. Section 40(2) says all premium must be paid “sambært §33, stk. 1”. Read that express reference together with §33\'s specific Sp/F sentence: apply the same paid proportion to Sp/F cash premium, while P/F premium remains fully payable. The literal “all premium” sentence in §40 is visible; this worksheet selects the specific §33 incorporation reading, rather than claiming a separate Registrar ruling. With DKK 200,000 Sp/F subscribed capital and DKK 100,000 premium, the minimum 25% capital payment is DKK 50,000 and corresponding premium payment DKK 25,000, for **DKK 75,000** total. The alternative isolated full-premium reading would require DKK 150,000. At the DKK 50,000 minimum capital, all capital is paid, so a DKK 20,000 premium is also fully paid: total DKK 70,000. Any noncash contribution requires full capital and premium under §33; it does not use this cash-only fraction. Retain the subscription, actual paid proportion, per-share reconciliation and payment evidence. [Companies Act §§33, 40][company]

A threshold comparison is not an audit-election approval.'''
edit(form,old,new)
